WEBVTT

00:00.970 --> 00:02.270
What was that scream?

00:02.270 --> 00:03.750
Didn’t it come from over here?

00:04.910 --> 00:06.120
Ayu!

00:09.410 --> 00:11.190
Why from over here?

00:11.780 --> 00:13.180
Ayu!

00:25.800 --> 00:26.760
Ayu?

00:28.750 --> 00:30.170
Are you here?

00:32.970 --> 00:34.050
Ayu?

00:35.170 --> 00:36.680
What’s the matter?

00:36.680 --> 00:38.530
What are you doing in...

00:49.450 --> 00:50.480
It’s too late.

00:51.070 --> 00:52.150
Ayu!

00:52.150 --> 00:53.570
What the hell happened?!

00:53.570 --> 00:54.610
Ayu!

00:54.610 --> 00:57.740
DEMON PRINCE ENMA

01:10.210 --> 01:12.210
PRODUCED BY: KAZUMI KAWASHIRO

01:16.020 --> 01:17.920
She’s the first to fall victim...

01:17.920 --> 01:19.180
What?

01:19.180 --> 01:21.180
PLANNED BY: DYNAMIC PLANNING

01:19.700 --> 01:21.180
What do you mean?

01:21.180 --> 01:22.570
She was murdered!

01:22.570 --> 01:23.890
That much is obvious!

01:24.290 --> 01:27.100
Having trapped us all in here,
they’re going to kill us off one by one!

01:27.110 --> 01:29.110
ORIGINAL STORY BY: GO NAGAI

01:27.550 --> 01:29.110
Miss Hoin, calm down!

01:29.560 --> 01:31.820
There is no evidence
that Miss Ayukawa was murdered.

01:31.860 --> 01:33.820
SCREENPLAY BY: TAKAWO YOSHIOKA

01:32.290 --> 01:33.820
Evidence?

01:34.120 --> 01:37.530
Well, she has no external wounds,
it could be an illness or something...

01:37.530 --> 01:39.870
Is evidence really necessary?

01:37.820 --> 01:39.870
CHARACTER DESIGN BY:
TOSHIYUKI KOMARU

01:37.820 --> 01:39.870
MONSTER DESIGN & ANIMATION DIRECTED BY: RYO TANAKA

01:39.870 --> 01:42.330
In this inconceivable situation!

01:42.330 --> 01:44.330
ART SETTING: TOMOYUKI AOKI

01:42.330 --> 01:44.330
ART DIRECTOR: KAZUHIRO ARAI

01:42.330 --> 01:44.330
COLOR SETTING: SACHIKO HARADA

01:45.040 --> 01:47.040
Ayu was murdered...

01:48.880 --> 01:50.080
Don’t move it.

01:50.080 --> 01:51.080
Huh?

01:50.090 --> 01:52.090
DIRECTOR OF
PHOTOGRAPHY:
KEISUKE TAKAHASHI
(STUDIO A-CAT)

01:50.090 --> 01:52.090
FILM EDITING:
MEGUMI UCHIDA

01:51.620 --> 01:54.340
We still don’t know whether it was
a natural death or a murder.

01:54.340 --> 01:56.050
Oh, you mean to conserve the crime scene?

01:56.050 --> 01:58.050
Yeah, I’m with the police.

01:58.050 --> 02:00.110
Don’t make me laugh!

01:58.800 --> 02:00.800
MUSIC BY: KAYO KONISHI
.........................YUKIO KONDO

01:58.800 --> 02:00.800
MUSIC PRODUCER: SHUNJI INOUE

02:00.110 --> 02:02.620
You’re helpless,
trapped in a place like this!

02:02.620 --> 02:05.090
But now you want to pull rank,
because you’re a cop?

02:07.020 --> 02:10.060
SOUND DIRECTOR:
KATSUNORI SHIMIZU

02:07.020 --> 02:10.060
SOUND EFFECTS: MUTSUHIRO NISHIMURA
(FIZZ SOUND CREATION)

02:07.800 --> 02:13.370
Hey Detective, given the situation,
why shouldn’t we consider her feelings?

02:18.240 --> 02:21.200
LINE PRODUCERS: KICHO MINAMI (BEE MEDIA)
............................................TATSUYOSHI KOBAYASHI

02:18.240 --> 02:21.200
ASSISTANT PRODUCER: ICHINAO NAGAI

02:22.580 --> 02:25.580
PRODUCERS:

02:22.580 --> 02:25.580
YASHIMA TOKUHARA

02:22.580 --> 02:25.580
SATSUKI MIZUNO

02:22.580 --> 02:25.580
YOSHIHIKO FUJISAWA

02:25.580 --> 02:29.310
I’m sorry. I’ll come back to get you soon.

02:31.350 --> 02:33.290
Please at least let me lie her down.

02:43.010 --> 02:45.970
DIRECTED BY: MAMORU KANBE

02:54.310 --> 02:56.150
What? What?

02:57.250 --> 03:00.150
I’m almost sure... there was a wall here...

03:01.800 --> 03:02.910
What are we going to do?

03:06.740 --> 03:07.660
Hey, wait!

03:08.390 --> 03:11.580
Walking around in circles
won’t get us anywhere.

03:11.580 --> 03:12.870
Those who want to come, come.

04:12.330 --> 04:13.440
Stay here.

04:27.240 --> 04:28.520
Are you okay?

04:44.420 --> 04:46.720
I knew it, this place is a hospital.

04:46.720 --> 04:49.400
In any case, we can rest here.

05:47.220 --> 05:47.990
Yoshinaga.

05:48.480 --> 05:51.120
We’ll take turns
keeping watch outside the room.

05:51.120 --> 05:53.440
Y-Yeah. That sounds good.

05:53.440 --> 05:54.760
You go ahead and rest first.

06:02.330 --> 06:06.720
Um... Wouldn’t it be good
for you to rest, too?

06:06.720 --> 06:08.610
Just leave me alone, okay.

06:11.910 --> 06:13.530
She was your best friend, right?

06:15.780 --> 06:17.330
We’ve been friends since we were kids.

06:18.460 --> 06:24.120
She was always being teased,
so I shield her...

06:25.100 --> 06:27.380
I told her I’d protect her, but...

06:31.790 --> 06:32.840
She...

06:33.960 --> 06:37.330
Wasn’t she terribly afraid
of the sound of a piano?

06:41.910 --> 06:47.140
When she was a girl
she was learning piano...

06:47.880 --> 06:51.930
and her teacher at the time
committed suicide.

06:52.340 --> 06:53.260
Suicide?

06:53.260 --> 06:58.610
The teacher, she was
a promising pianist...

06:58.610 --> 07:02.900
I don’t know the details, but it seems
she suffered a major finger injury.

07:04.750 --> 07:08.510
I guess that must have been
a great shock to Ayu.

07:08.510 --> 07:11.960
She seems to have been scared
of pianos since then.

07:14.840 --> 07:16.410
A kind of wound of the heart...

07:16.410 --> 07:17.620
A wound of the heart...

07:19.610 --> 07:20.830
What is it?

07:20.830 --> 07:23.610
I can’t just take a rest
and leave her alone.

07:23.610 --> 07:24.340
Hey, wait!

07:25.020 --> 07:26.870
Let go of me!

07:25.320 --> 07:26.870
No, don’t go!

07:26.870 --> 07:27.590
What’s going on?

07:27.590 --> 07:28.730
Well...

07:28.730 --> 07:29.670
Oh, don’t!

07:33.220 --> 07:34.860
She said she’s going to the piano room!

07:34.860 --> 07:35.780
Shit!

07:37.220 --> 07:40.470
Get Yoshinaga to keep watch outside,
you get inside.

07:40.470 --> 07:41.330
Understand?

07:41.330 --> 07:42.190
Y-Yeah.

07:51.200 --> 07:52.950
EMAIL

07:51.200 --> 07:52.950
You've got mail
from Mr.Sosuke.

07:53.980 --> 07:55.450
That’s enough!

07:55.980 --> 07:59.620
I’m sorry, but I’ve set my phone
to refuse your E-mails.

07:59.620 --> 08:01.120
Wh-Why did you?

08:01.120 --> 08:02.160
Sosuke!

08:02.640 --> 08:04.240
I...

08:05.390 --> 08:07.670
I never agreed to us splitting up!

08:07.670 --> 08:10.850
We discussed and agreed to it...

08:10.850 --> 08:13.420
but you keep on moping about.

08:13.420 --> 08:17.430
To be honest, I don’t even want
to look at a guy like you.

08:17.780 --> 08:19.390
Damn it! Damn it!

08:20.790 --> 08:22.270
What are you doing?

08:23.400 --> 08:25.480
I’ll die, I’ll die for you!

08:25.480 --> 08:27.430
That’ll make you happy, right?

08:30.950 --> 08:32.960
Oh cut it out.

08:33.520 --> 08:36.070
You said you were going
to jump in front of a train before.

08:36.520 --> 08:38.830
Don’t you think that’s just
the worst kind of threat?

08:39.270 --> 08:41.300
I really will kill myself!

08:44.360 --> 08:46.010
Fine, do what you want.

08:53.550 --> 08:55.550
Roster 3-A

08:53.550 --> 08:55.550
Home Room Teacher
Sosuke Oshiba

09:05.940 --> 09:07.980
You did it.

09:11.020 --> 09:12.760
Who would do this?

09:33.150 --> 09:36.130
So in this case the formula is...

09:39.020 --> 09:41.870
So in this case the formula is...

09:53.030 --> 09:55.730
I will kill you all.

10:11.510 --> 10:13.310
Making a fool out of me,

10:14.500 --> 10:16.830
all of them making a fool of me.

10:17.470 --> 10:17.510
I will kill you all.

10:24.560 --> 10:27.560
Making... a fool of me.

10:31.970 --> 10:33.620
It’s been so long....

10:39.340 --> 10:41.730
Mr. Yoshinaga, where is everyone?

10:45.160 --> 10:46.330
Mr. Yoshinaga?

10:46.780 --> 10:49.820
There is no way out of here anyway.

10:49.820 --> 10:51.170
Everyone will die.

10:51.510 --> 10:52.360
What’s the matter?

10:52.360 --> 10:53.710
Shut up!

10:53.710 --> 10:56.740
I was thinking I’d kill you sometime!

10:56.740 --> 11:00.220
You all treat me like a fool...!

11:16.730 --> 11:17.990
You!

11:41.220 --> 11:43.850
Finally you reveal yourself.

11:47.480 --> 11:49.270
Murderer

11:49.950 --> 11:51.160
Why?

11:51.160 --> 11:52.280
Who is this?

12:01.820 --> 12:02.860
No!

12:11.410 --> 12:12.780
You?

12:30.300 --> 12:32.050
Don’t mess with me!

12:36.520 --> 12:38.300
Oh, no...

12:49.970 --> 12:51.410
What is this?

12:52.080 --> 12:53.200
Why?

12:53.780 --> 12:55.320
Where’s my jacket?

12:55.320 --> 12:57.100
Where’s my hat? My shoes?

13:11.590 --> 13:15.020
There was no... door like this before.

13:20.970 --> 13:22.400
A basement...

13:27.240 --> 13:28.300
Why?

14:33.260 --> 14:35.780
What is this room?

15:11.010 --> 15:13.800
I guess someone lives here?

15:25.530 --> 15:27.070
There’s only this?

15:56.890 --> 15:56.930
Kiyoshi

16:00.730 --> 16:01.990
Boss Yuri!

16:03.020 --> 16:05.290
It’s seriously dangerous tonight!

16:05.290 --> 16:07.500
The cops are on patrol all over the town.

16:07.500 --> 16:08.820
You idiot!

16:10.370 --> 16:13.460
Yuri Benten won’t be so easy to catch!

16:14.460 --> 16:16.330
Screw this checkpoint!

16:16.330 --> 16:17.620
We’ve got the guts to just break through it!

16:18.080 --> 16:19.190
Yeah!

16:22.620 --> 16:23.540
No! I said, “No!”

17:29.080 --> 17:30.880
Yo-You?

17:34.640 --> 17:37.530
They feed on
the darkness of the human heart.

17:49.450 --> 17:50.090
Darkness?

17:50.540 --> 17:54.510
“She seems to have been scared
of pianos since then.”

17:55.850 --> 17:57.510
“A kind of wound of the heart.”

17:58.010 --> 18:01.610
“They feed on the darkness of the human heart.”

18:01.610 --> 18:02.840
Oh no!

18:03.480 --> 18:04.140
Everyone’s in danger!

18:14.160 --> 18:16.490
Kikuko... sorry.

18:59.860 --> 19:01.450
Over there!

19:05.450 --> 19:07.540
This place is...!

19:18.550 --> 19:21.030
No!

19:55.690 --> 19:57.370
I didn’t make it in time...

19:58.430 --> 20:00.510
She must have had some darkness, too...

20:02.340 --> 20:04.020
That’s why she was taken...

20:30.570 --> 20:32.200
I won’t be duped.

20:43.030 --> 20:44.070
What happened?

20:46.250 --> 20:47.610
Hang on!

20:47.610 --> 20:48.380
Are you alright?

20:48.380 --> 20:49.640
Y-Yeah.

20:49.640 --> 20:50.870
What happened?

20:50.870 --> 20:52.650
I don’t know.

20:52.650 --> 20:55.270
Mr. Yoshinaga attacked me...

20:55.270 --> 20:58.460
and I... I don’t know...

20:58.460 --> 21:00.040
Are you hurt?

21:00.040 --> 21:02.360
And why are you dressed like that?

21:03.060 --> 21:04.370
Darkness.

21:04.370 --> 21:05.400
What?

21:06.100 --> 21:07.620
A wound of the heart...

21:08.570 --> 21:13.750
There’s something here that takes advantage
of the darkness of our hearts and hunts our very lives...

21:14.250 --> 21:19.840
Miss Ayukawa and Miss Hoin too...
it devoured, their souls.

21:19.840 --> 21:21.630
Devoured their souls?

21:23.100 --> 21:24.420
What is all this?

21:25.390 --> 21:28.090
That is my question!

21:28.090 --> 21:30.510
But common sense no longer applies!

21:30.840 --> 21:34.750
This place too... there’s no doubt
the layout is changing every moment.

21:35.580 --> 21:37.640
A woman in a white kimono.

21:37.640 --> 21:38.480
Huh?

21:41.480 --> 21:43.010
I saw her.

21:43.950 --> 21:46.830
She must still be
hiding somewhere here.

21:47.640 --> 21:50.920
There might also be a man in a black cloak.

21:50.920 --> 21:51.490
What?

21:52.120 --> 21:56.410
I met him... I guess.

21:56.920 --> 22:01.040
It was like a dream or an illusion...
so I can’t be too sure.

22:01.560 --> 22:06.010
Anyway, us survivors
should stick together...

22:08.860 --> 22:10.010
Hmmm, Yoshinaga...

22:11.130 --> 22:13.070
It was him that attacked you then?

22:13.070 --> 22:14.670
He was no longer a person....

22:14.670 --> 22:15.570
What?

22:15.570 --> 22:18.010
It wasn’t a person,
it was like a monster.

22:18.010 --> 22:21.020
So perhaps he became a monster.

22:21.020 --> 22:22.060
Huh?

22:22.580 --> 22:23.980
Just as you said...

22:23.980 --> 22:28.010
my common sense doesn’t work jack shit here.

22:29.350 --> 22:33.790
I have to believe what I’ve seen
with my own eyes.

22:51.980 --> 22:52.720
Yoshinaga!

22:54.400 --> 22:55.850
Kill them all!

22:55.850 --> 23:00.020
All those rotten brats,
all of them will face my punishment!

23:03.150 --> 23:06.850
Before... you came to
interview me, didn’t you?

23:06.850 --> 23:07.950
Huh?

23:07.950 --> 23:09.280
About vampires and stuff?

23:10.330 --> 23:11.860
They’re all the same.

23:11.860 --> 23:14.900
After the incidents,
all the suspects from the cases...

23:14.900 --> 23:16.660
they all went mad like this.

23:17.540 --> 23:20.800
It’s as if something departed from them
and took their souls.

23:20.800 --> 23:21.920
Which means...

23:22.280 --> 23:26.630
The whatever it is that turned them into
monsters might exist separately.

23:27.050 --> 23:30.970
So assuming that’s the cause of this
series of suspicious incidents, it’s...

23:43.890 --> 23:49.150
All of them, they all call me
things like the Perv-naga!

23:49.660 --> 23:55.520
Yes! Those pigs,
what does it matter if I kill them.

24:10.900 --> 24:12.200
“Inspector Abashiri.”

24:12.830 --> 24:14.460
“No smoking at the crime scene.”

24:15.560 --> 24:16.730
Oyamada...

24:20.260 --> 24:23.520
I guess you were right.

24:27.170 --> 24:28.850
I’ll just use this for now...

24:38.650 --> 24:40.870
If you can’t flee
you’ve got to fight.

24:41.590 --> 24:42.620
Right?

24:43.250 --> 24:44.460
Okay, I’ll be back later.

24:45.020 --> 24:47.540
Demons that feed on the darkness
of the human heart...

24:47.880 --> 24:51.870
In me, in anyone
something like that exists...

24:52.590 --> 24:54.180
But you’ll lose
if you let them see your weakness.

25:21.940 --> 25:23.330
What’s... this?

25:27.560 --> 25:31.470
Three out of the five have
turned into skull faces...

25:32.770 --> 25:35.500
Two women and one man...

25:36.140 --> 25:37.670
You understand what this means, yeah?

25:38.810 --> 25:41.150
The remaining man is you, Detective,

25:41.150 --> 25:43.030
and the last woman... that’s me...

25:44.500 --> 25:47.230
Wait, there was one more person,

25:47.230 --> 25:49.070
the one you’re worried about...

25:50.620 --> 25:52.400
So that’s where it was hiding...

26:00.170 --> 26:02.490
Detective, help me.

26:04.070 --> 26:05.260
Detective...

26:05.930 --> 26:07.180
Help me...

26:14.780 --> 26:18.490
De-Detective... Help... me.

26:19.850 --> 26:21.120
Detective...

26:25.120 --> 26:27.520
Detective, help me.

26:28.090 --> 26:29.420
Detective.

26:35.100 --> 26:37.520
Brother, help me.

26:38.860 --> 26:40.640
Let her go Goda.

26:40.640 --> 26:42.240
What’s the point of doing this?

26:42.240 --> 26:47.790
I’m going to make you feel the same way I did
when my brother was killed.

26:47.790 --> 26:48.830
Right, Detective?

26:49.340 --> 26:53.880
Your brother killed five innocent people.

26:53.880 --> 26:57.500
And he almost managed to commit the sixth murder...

26:57.500 --> 26:59.520
right in front of me.

26:59.520 --> 27:04.600
Yes, then it will be me who commits
the murder my brother was incapable of.

27:04.600 --> 27:06.930
A murder right before your eyes!

27:06.930 --> 27:07.310
Don’t shoot!

27:08.480 --> 27:11.370
Don’t shoot!`

27:18.420 --> 27:20.410
Got you!

27:24.380 --> 27:25.630
I’m sorry...

27:26.420 --> 27:28.580
I’m so sorry Kikuko.

27:28.580 --> 27:30.160
De-Detective.

27:30.480 --> 27:34.170
Don’t be... taken by... the darkness...

27:34.170 --> 27:35.370
Detective...

27:48.200 --> 27:49.770
Found you.

28:10.760 --> 28:12.040
Y-You!

28:16.830 --> 28:17.960
Enma!

28:26.010 --> 28:29.720
Haven’t you grown since we last met?

28:30.950 --> 28:33.730
That woman came along
at just the right time.

28:34.170 --> 28:37.390
I copied your trick, possessing her.

28:38.040 --> 28:42.230
By the way, possessing people is more
exhausting than expected huh?

28:42.820 --> 28:44.490
I won’t let you get away this time.

28:52.670 --> 28:53.840
What’s with this thing?!

28:53.840 --> 28:56.710
This energy...
I can’t believe it, but it’s...

29:01.380 --> 29:02.440
Enma!

29:21.030 --> 29:23.030
Wha-What happened?!

29:38.480 --> 29:40.170
Detective, hold on!

29:40.470 --> 29:42.940
I’ll never forgive you!

29:55.260 --> 29:56.460
Detective...

29:57.260 --> 29:58.550
hold on...

30:49.780 --> 30:50.900
Enma!

30:52.920 --> 30:54.040
What the hell is this!

30:54.040 --> 30:57.360
It’s growing more than we expected.

30:57.360 --> 31:00.800
This thing gobbled up
quite a lot of darkness.

31:00.800 --> 31:02.120
Shit!

31:06.760 --> 31:07.510
Yuki-chan!

31:07.510 --> 31:08.340
Enma, no!

31:08.340 --> 31:09.720
Shit!

31:14.110 --> 31:16.750
It grows every time someone dies...

31:17.820 --> 31:20.980
This is its feeding ground...

31:26.080 --> 31:27.190
Enma...

31:29.520 --> 31:30.600
Enma...

31:32.490 --> 31:33.640
Enma...

31:35.490 --> 31:36.520
I’m sorry.

31:37.440 --> 31:38.590
Yuki-chan.

31:39.130 --> 31:42.380
I... I love you Enma.

31:44.390 --> 31:47.110
But, I am... snow...

31:48.940 --> 31:50.510
and you are flame...

31:51.910 --> 31:55.350
We’ll never be able to be together,
for all eternity, I just can’t bear it...

31:56.380 --> 31:57.370
Sorry.

31:58.110 --> 31:59.180
I’m sorry.

32:00.050 --> 32:01.630
What are you talking about?

32:02.240 --> 32:04.430
Sometimes I can hear something whispering...

32:05.470 --> 32:11.400
if you and me evaporate together forever...

32:12.330 --> 32:13.470
I’m sorry...

32:15.250 --> 32:22.260
Somewhere along the way I came
to think it might be alright...

32:22.260 --> 32:23.340
Hold on!

32:23.340 --> 32:24.400
Sorry.

32:25.420 --> 32:26.410
Enma.

32:27.380 --> 32:28.670
I’m sorry.

32:31.470 --> 32:36.860
Let’s become one and melt away together, shall we?

32:36.860 --> 32:39.440
Please, Enma.

32:39.440 --> 32:41.360
Yu-Yukihime.

32:42.310 --> 32:43.840
Chapeauji!

32:46.270 --> 32:47.320
Kapaeru?!

32:49.200 --> 32:54.640
Hey boss... you were brutal
to sacrifice me...

32:54.640 --> 32:56.820
with you the sole survivor.

32:57.150 --> 32:58.180
Sacrifice?

32:58.180 --> 32:58.910
What are you...

32:58.910 --> 33:02.430
If you hadn’t left all by yourself...

33:02.430 --> 33:06.480
Sat-chan and myself
wouldn’t have to have died...

33:06.480 --> 33:07.500
You’re wrong!

33:13.130 --> 33:15.560
It’s okay, don’t suffer...

33:16.210 --> 33:17.800
so...

33:17.800 --> 33:20.310
let’s go to Kapaeru.

33:22.570 --> 33:26.800
If you and I can become one together...

33:27.430 --> 33:29.070
that’s good enough.

33:29.070 --> 33:32.230
It’s what we’ve always been hoping for.

33:51.350 --> 33:52.710
Just kidding.

33:53.250 --> 33:56.410
He is the King of the Afterlife’s nephew.

33:57.190 --> 33:59.720
He holds no light nor darkness.

34:00.770 --> 34:02.380
Will you come with me...

34:02.380 --> 34:04.320
or be destroyed right here...

34:04.320 --> 34:07.420
Nah, you don’t get to choose,

34:07.420 --> 34:08.480
you die right here!

34:32.210 --> 34:34.720
Chapeauji, what the hell’s this?

34:34.720 --> 34:36.920
I see.

34:36.920 --> 34:39.550
Hiding in Yukihime’s body...

34:39.550 --> 34:45.350
it absorbed every last bit of darkness
from all the victims we met.

34:45.350 --> 34:47.530
That’s why the faces looked familiar.

35:04.270 --> 35:06.030
Who are you?

35:07.180 --> 35:11.650
Even if you did know,
it would not have mattered...

35:11.650 --> 35:15.880
The best you can do is be aware of
the darkness within your own heart.

35:15.880 --> 35:16.880
Huh?

35:19.550 --> 35:21.520
What happened to me?

35:21.520 --> 35:23.340
You were sleeping.

35:23.340 --> 35:24.680
Sleeping?

35:25.340 --> 35:26.840
Where’s Kapaeru?

35:26.840 --> 35:28.390
I can’t see him.

35:35.220 --> 35:36.590
Be at ease...

35:38.000 --> 35:39.700
I avenged him.

35:39.700 --> 35:41.100
Avenged?

35:41.100 --> 35:42.240
Let’s go home.

35:48.890 --> 35:50.460
Hey, wait!

35:50.930 --> 35:52.210
Don’t just leave me here!

36:03.650 --> 36:04.780
Why?

36:11.350 --> 36:13.430
No, no way.

36:33.670 --> 36:33.710
ENMA

36:54.000 --> 37:01.940
In the darkness of night, laying in bed
Tonight also, ever deeper decadence

37:01.940 --> 37:11.740
Smeared with grotesque make-up
Heart and body soaked, so upside-down

37:13.350 --> 37:16.110
Upside-down

37:18.820 --> 37:26.990
Make you, make me thrilled
Under the moonlight, honey

37:26.990 --> 37:34.580
Spit upon the bound-up heart

37:34.580 --> 37:42.310
Do the trip
Come on let’s dance, mired in depravity

37:42.310 --> 37:51.460
In return for this degradation,
unhidden jealous heart

37:51.460 --> 37:55.580
Body lusting for riot

38:08.820 --> 38:09.600
Whoa...

38:09.600 --> 38:11.430
Hey, what a cool old place.

38:11.430 --> 38:13.190
C’mon, let’s not do this.

38:13.190 --> 38:15.780
It’s just a rumor.

38:15.780 --> 38:17.190
This place is messed up, I mean it.

38:18.040 --> 38:19.940
I’m telling you,
someone has really seen it.

38:20.360 --> 38:22.470
A ghost of a woman in a red dress.

38:22.470 --> 38:24.510
I don’t see anything.

38:25.940 --> 38:27.950
Someone has come...

38:28.540 --> 38:30.280
C’mon, let’s get out of here.

38:30.280 --> 38:32.580
God, don’t be such a wimp.

38:39.660 --> 38:40.690
Hey...

38:40.690 --> 38:42.520
Don’t leave me here...

38:42.520 --> 38:44.170
I’m not dead...

38:45.060 --> 38:46.470
I’m not dead...

38:47.050 --> 38:48.840
so don’t leave me...

38:49.640 --> 38:53.200
Please don’t leave me...
